GLM'S CONDITIONAL ESCAPE IS REFUTED BY MEASUREMENT, in both polarities: `default:''s refusal conditioned on idata is
killed by the population-1 LOAD rows when the condition is `idata != 0' (a read carries idata 0, dev_vme.c:73/:75-76)
and by the STORE rows when it is `idata == 0' (every population-1 store the probe makes is non-zero: WVAL at 0x90,
NARROW and DHI:DLO in `p1 widths').  It was never a floor survivor; GLM's packet did not carry the probe's store values.

M_DIRODATA -- THE PREDICTION'S REASON WAS WEAKER THAN THE TRUTH, corrected here.  PRETABLE2C said the leg is
"equivalent on the sample" because nothing writes the population-2 words of d->reg[].  The binary says more: odata is
assigned ONLY on a read (dev_vme.c:78-79, `if (writeflag == MEM_READ) odata = d->reg[...]'), so on the write path the
conjunct `!(odata & 2)' is the constant `!(0 & 2)', and GCC 15.2.1 -O3 folded it -- the leg compiles to the fix's own
binary.  It is an EQUIVALENT MUTANT in every execution, not a sampled slice: the odata half of the clause-(e) store-data
family GLM named does not exist for the direction test.  (A conjunct on idata, table 2b's M_IDATABIT1, is different:
idata is live on the write path and its binary differs.)

